# What Docker must NOT send as build context.
#
# WITHOUT THIS FILE the context is ~777 MB -- the whole repository, including
# 351 MB of apps/web/node_modules that no image uses. On a normal disk that is
# merely wasteful. On this working tree, which is iCloud-synced, it is fatal:
# a build sat for twenty minutes without producing a layer, because the daemon
# was still reading the context. Production builds images on the box
# (docs/DEPLOY.md), so this is a deploy-time cost, not just a laptop one.
#
# Keep in step with what the Dockerfiles actually COPY:
#   apps/api/{*.py,alembic.ini,migrations}   apps/web/   libs/   services/
#   shared/{tiers,policy-fields}.json        scripts/security/

# Version control
.git
.git.nosync
.gitignore

# Node. The web image runs its own `npm ci` and then COPY apps/web/ -- so
# shipping the host's node_modules is not just slow, it OVERWRITES a correct
# install with binaries built for the host's platform.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/npm-debug.log*

# Python caches and virtualenvs
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv
**/venv

# Local databases. apps/api defaults to sqlite:///./aiprotect.db, so a
# developer who has run the API has one of these sitting next to the source.
# It must never be baked into an image.
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# Secrets. Belt and braces -- these should never be here, and if one is, it
# must not become an image layer.
.env
.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Documentation and working material: never COPYed, always sent.
docs/
demo-videos/
demo-range-prompts/
**/*.pdf
**/*.docx

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
